<InfoPage title="Editorial Policy" kicker="How we publish" description="Standards for original Dreemy AI comparisons, primary sources, updates, privacy boundaries, and corrections."><h2>Answer the decision</h2><p>Every page should help with a concrete choice. Keywords appear in descriptive titles, headings, direct answers, and natural explanations—not hidden blocks or repetitive filler.</p><h2>Primary sources first</h2><p>Product claims should link to official pages when available. Privacy guidance relies on recognized primary resources. We identify uncertainty and tell readers when a live product check is necessary.</p><h2>Clear adult boundaries</h2><p>Adult character-chat coverage emphasizes consenting-adult fictional scenarios, privacy, cost visibility, and emotional boundaries. We never request private conversations, credentials, or intimate personal media.</p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>Material changes update the visible revision date. Correction requests should identify the URL, disputed text, and a direct source supporting the change.</p></InfoPage>
